faqs:
  - q: Are GullStack websites HIPAA compliant for medical practices?
    a: We build HIPAA-mindful websites with encrypted data transmission, secure hosting, and privacy-first design. Our websites do not store protected health information directly. For patient scheduling, intake forms, and patient portals, we integrate with HIPAA-compliant systems and can sign Business Associate Agreements where needed. We work with practices to ensure every patient touchpoint meets compliance requirements.
  - q: Can patients book appointments directly through the website?
    a: Yes. We build online scheduling directly into your website. Patients see real-time availability, choose their provider and appointment type, and book instantly. Automatic confirmation emails and text reminders reduce no-shows by up to 90 percent. The system integrates with your existing practice management software so your staff does not have to manage two calendars.
  - q: How do you handle patient reviews without violating privacy?
    a: We set up automated review request systems that invite patients to share their experience on Google after their visit. The system never references specific treatments or conditions. We also build your website to showcase existing reviews prominently, which builds trust with new patients researching your practice. Managing your online reputation is essential since 77 percent of patients check reviews before booking.
  - q: What kind of medical practices do you work with?
    a: We work with general practitioners, dentists, orthodontists, chiropractors, dermatologists, physical therapists, optometrists, pediatricians, and other specialty practices. Our systems are flexible enough to handle multi-provider practices with different scheduling needs, insurance information pages, and provider directories.
  - q: Do you integrate with existing practice management systems?
    a: Yes. We integrate with popular practice management systems including Athenahealth, DrChrono, Dentrix, Open Dental, ChiroTouch, and others. Our goal is to complement your existing workflow, not replace it. We handle the marketing, website, and patient acquisition side while your PMS handles the clinical side.
